## Going live: connect the request form

Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and set `VITE_FORM_ENDPOINT` to any endpoint that
accepts a JSON POST (Formspree, Basin, a CRM webhook, or your own API), then
rebuild. Without it, the form runs in demo mode: it validates and shows the
success message, and logs the request to the browser console.

## Before launch: confirm the selling points

The site only says what the business has confirmed. The claims that most
reduce a caller's risk are switched off in `confirmed` in
`src/data/content.js` until the owner confirms them. Once filled in, each
one appears automatically in the trust bar, hero, About section, and FAQ.

| Setting | What to confirm with the owner | Where it appears |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `license` | License type and number | Trust bar, hero, About, FAQ |
| `insured` | Liability insurance in force | Trust bar, hero, About, FAQ |
| `upfrontPricing` | Do customers always approve the price before work starts? | Trust bar, hero, pricing FAQ |
| `warranty` | Written warranty terms, exactly as offered | Trust bar, FAQ |
| `reviews` | Real rating, review count, and profile link | Next to the hero buttons |

Also before launch:

- Replace the three placeholder testimonials with verified reviews (with
  customer permission) and remove `isPlaceholder`.
- Confirm the email address (marked `VERIFY`).
- Swap the van illustration for a real photo of the owner, team, or truck.
- If the business offers after-hours emergency service, say so in
  `business.schedule`, `EmergencyBanner.jsx`, and the FAQ. The site
  currently assumes phones are staffed only Mon–Sat, 7 AM–8 PM.
- Link a privacy policy near the forms if the business has one.

## Measuring calls and leads

Phone calls are the main goal, so every `tel:` link is tracked automatically.
Add Google Analytics 4 (gtag) or Google Tag Manager to `index.html` and these
events start flowing, with no code changes needed:

- `phone_call_click` with `location`: `top` (hero), `services`, `emergency`,
  `about`, `why-us`, `service-area`, `faq`, `contact`, `header`, `footer`, or
  `sticky-bar`
- `lead_submit` with `location` (`hero` or `contact`) and `service`

In development, events are logged to the browser console.

